  "notes": ["The three original STIH blocks come from unedited AFS member 473. The original relocator edits only guest copies; all triangle bytes and resolved list references are checked. In the empty-secondary controls only the first reference of each secondary list is replaced with a sentinel.","The stage object bounds and Sasuke rigid poses are declared. Only Sasuke's normal role-08 sphere and ordinary capsule publish. The isolated solver and the enclosing walk up to presentation agree on root, vector, flags and broad centers; allocated capsule endpoints and HP are unchanged.","The three targeted sites include positive X, negative X, and positive Z. The reported face projection calls show source triangle ordinals, not a claim that every projection produced a correction. Null in the bounded sample denotes a different call site.","The stored plane anchor does not reproduce vertex tangency. A sphere exactly 50 units from the vertex sets both flags with zero displacement; one positive outward binary32 step misses and one inward step is corrected. Starting at the same final pose behind the wall is distinct from crossing it.","This is original static stage geometry under bounded poses, not a live retail arena tick, dynamic stage construction, drawing, original hardware or native gameplay."],
